Z||000009||Tigger||01-22-2001||09:02 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cheever2:<BR><B>Tigger, did you take that pic?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yep. It was cool, er, awesome to see.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>From what I hear, Jaguar is the first team to show their car for the upcoming season.  Overall the car isn't much different from last year just looking at it from the outside, but I've heard they've made some improvements especially in the rear suspension.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Cheever2||01-22-2001||10:42 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ray b:<BR>nascar lost me when it became kitcars with no real stock layout<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Funny thing is, that's what a Nascar fan told me he doesn't like about open wheel racing - that it's nothing like regular cars.  Yeah, like Nascar is?  Shuh! As if! I know this will get some flames from someone, but that's just what one guy told me, okay?  Well, F1 is more like real racing competition the way it was meant to be, on the road, standing start, all-out.  What I don't like about it, as with ALL forms of racing, is the rules (the "formula") they put on them to keep the speeds down.  I say the innovations that have gone into racing over the years to get them fast - yet make it to the end of the race - are precisely what have led to some of the best advances in passenger cars: higher performance, better safety, endurance, technology and overall quality.  Don't put restrictions on those people, let's see how far they can go.  And if they go too fast for the tracks, build bigger tracks.  Better yet, close down portions of highway on an early Sunday morning.  With enough public notice it would be possible, besides, I prefer races on real roads.<BR>Okay, that's enough for now.<P>||||reg||6
Z||000011||Will||01-22-2001||11:21 AM||||You'd have to pick the roads carefully. An F1 car with 1" of ground clearance doesn't take potholes too well.<P>The rules are there to keep drivers safe. How many deaths do you think F1 would have each year if cars were touching 350 mph on the straights with 2500 horsepower?<P>I like F1 as much as the next guy, but I don't like to see drivers killed.||||reg||1
